Description: Boswas OS desktop: compositor, shell and session
 The native Boswas OS desktop, written in Rust. It takes the place of KWin,
 the Plasma shell and the Plasma session; applications keep working because
 it speaks the standard Wayland protocols, and X11 applications run through
 Xwayland.
 .
  * boswas-compositor: the display server, window manager and effects
    engine (on the Smithay library). Boswas window frames with rounded
    corners and shadows, animations, snap layouts, a window picker
    (Alt+Tab), Task View with several desktops, a window menu, fractional
    scaling, settings per monitor, night light, input methods, touch
    screens, touchpad gestures and drawing tablets; DRM/KMS with OpenGL ES
    on real hardware, a software renderer for tests
  * boswas-shell: the taskbar with Start, search, pinned and running
    applications, the tray and the clock; quick settings (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth,
    sound, brightness, power mode); notifications with a calendar; the
    volume and brightness display; screen capture; the polkit password
    dialog; the lock screen and the login screen
  * boswas-services-bridge: the shell's network, Bluetooth, sound and power
    backends for the Settings application
  * boswas-session: the session greetd starts after login
 .
 Security model: ordinary applications cannot read other windows or global
 key strokes. Panels, the lock screen, the window list, clipboard control
 and input methods are offered only to the programs the compositor starts
 itself; sandboxed applications never see them. A program gets pictures of
 the screen only after the user has allowed it. The compositor owns the
 session lock: a locked screen stays blank even if the lock screen crashes.
 The session locks after ten minutes without input, and a user cannot
 lengthen that.
 .
 greetd is pointed at /etc/boswas/greetd.toml by a systemd drop-in; its own
 configuration file is not modified.
